# CODEOWNERS — testing-os
#
# F-W1-CI-035: GitHub uses this file to require an owner review on PRs that
# touch listed paths. Pair with a branch-protection rule that requires
# CODEOWNERS review where needed. CLAUDE.md hard rule #9 ("match scrutiny to
# blast radius") frames the discipline: single-file changes can land
# directly, cross-cut surfaces deserve a review pass.
#
# Single-owner pattern — bring on additional owners by adding @-handles to
# specific paths once a second steward exists.

* @mcp-tool-shop

# Critical surfaces — these get explicit lines so that adding a future
# additional owner does NOT silently drop the existing CODEOWNER. The
# default rule above already covers these paths; the explicit lines are
# the documentation surface, not a security increment by themselves.
.github/workflows/      @mcp-tool-shop
.github/CODEOWNERS      @mcp-tool-shop
.github/dependabot.yml  @mcp-tool-shop
packages/schemas/       @mcp-tool-shop
policies/               @mcp-tool-shop
swarms/PROTOCOL.md      @mcp-tool-shop
